
// Below will be a 'Generator<uint32>' which will implement 'Iterable<uint32>'
val generator = () => {
    yield 1;
    yield 2;
    if (System.getTime().getHour() > 12) {
        yield break;
    }
    yield 3;
};

val consumer = () => {
    for v in generator() {
        System.println(`No-cost iterable: ${v}`);
    }
};

// Should it be possible somehow to have "labels" for what to yield back to
// How could we make this typesafe and call-safe, to *ensure* someone is listening to the yielded data?
// Or is that just stupid and it should be up to each caller to propagate the data further up?
// Or is this something that can be used together with the context parameters to point to what to send to?
